{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LsjZMvt5HASQKH5rYr24T8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Portfolio Program â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1)\n2\t\n3\t> North Star (LOCKED): Build a deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry â€” model-agnostic\n4\t> cognitive skills, compositional recipes, and (later) stateful agents â€” where every skill carries a\n5\t> LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions\n6\t> WITHOUT drifting from its designed purpose. First end-to-end proof: a recreate-a-paper recipe that\n7\t> REPRODUCES the Gelman ANOVA paper, GRADED ON ARCHITECTURE/HANDOFF SUCCESS (not reproduction fidelity).\n8\t\n9\tThis Master Plan covers ONE Foreman-ready plan set, executed as sequential per-skill WAVE-GROUPS, whose\n10\tFIRST executable wave is the Phase-0 shared infrastructure. Per-skill work here is lightweight (canary +\n11\tNorth-Star authoring), NOT a full separate researchPrime cycle (FIX-12); full per-skill cycles are for\n12\tLATER portfolio skills beyond this plan. The recreate-a-paper slice is the proof.\n13\t\n14\t> **Stage-1 Shark-Tank convergence (2026-06-20):** 3 Sharks found 3 â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs + 2 MAJORs.\n15\t> Scope fork resolved by the user (convergence authority): **BREADTH-FIRST** â€” this plan set builds all\n16\t> five cognitive skills to production depth (full canary sets + journals), THEN the recreate-a-paper slice.\n17\t> The four non-scope findings are folded into v2 below (see \"Shark-Tank fixes applied\").\n18\t\n19\t## Shark-Tank fixes applied (v2)\n20\t- **FIX-1 (BLOCKER: Foreman gate can't host LLM-judge/numeric validators):** all three validator types\n21\t  emit **Node-TAP / pytest output with real per-test PASS events** so Foreman's `runGate` counts them\n22\t  (no vacuous-green HALT). The TAP/pytest emitter IS the shared interface (also resolves FIX-4).\n23\t- **FIX-2 (BLOCKER: done-check not deterministic):** the architecture/handoff done-check is DEFINED NOW\n24\t  (see \"NS6 deterministic done-check\" below), not deferred.\n25\t- **FIX-3 (MAJOR: substrate spike has no gate):** P0.A opens with a **Wave-0 go/no-go spike** with an\n26\t  explicit fallback if Foreman-substrate hosting of wrapped validators fails.\n27\t- **FIX-4 (MAJOR: R6 shared interface unstated):** = the TAP/pytest emitter contract above.\n28\t- **FIX-5 (MAJOR: NS4 tier table doesn't exist/untested):** the logical-tierâ†’model table is a NET-NEW\n29\t  artifact built in P0.C **with a swap test** (swap the table â†’ assert the resolved model changes; no skill\n30\t  prose edited). Replaces the scattered per-role TRIO_MODEL_<ROLE> env resolution.\n31\t- **FIX-6 (carried: canary evolution):** canary sets are **versioned alongside skill versions**; a sleep\n32\t  cycle may PROPOSE canary additions but never edit/delete existing canaries (append-only; a deletion is a\n33\t  human call) â€” so the set neither ossifies (NS1) nor is silently weakened (NS2).\n34\t- **FIX-7 (carried: A1 fallback honesty):** the deterministic-only fallback is valid ONLY for validator (iii)\n35\t  and deterministic (ii) canaries; for LLM-judged (ii) canaries an unreachable cross-family host **HALTs as\n36\t  a degraded-coverage stamp**, never silently scores same-family.\n37\t\n38\t## Shark-Tank fixes applied (v3 â€” round 2 convergence)\n39\tRound 2 (substrate-verified) found the v2 gate was sound in plumbing but unsound in semantics. v3 folds\n40\tONE governing principle + targeted fixes:\n41\t\n42\t- **PRINCIPLE-D (the deterministic-gate rule â€” resolves flaky-gate + HALT-incoherence):** the no-regression\n43\t  GATE emits TAP `ok`/`not ok` ONLY from DETERMINISTIC checks (numeric tolerance, code/unit tests, path/schema\n44\t  existence). **LLM-judge and cross-family judging are ADVISORY** â€” they write a report artifact recorded\n45\t  alongside the wave, and NEVER emit a gate verdict. Consequences: (a) a non-deterministic judge can no longer\n46\t  flip the gate GREENâ†”HALT (round-2 CLUSTER A); (b) an unreachable cross-family host can no longer HALT the\n47\t  build â€” it just records \"degraded advisory coverage\" (corrects the false v2 FIX-7; Foreman HALT is terminal,\n48\t  so judging must stay OUT of the gate path). The cross-family judge still runs when reachable; its value is a\n49\t  recorded second-origin signal, not a gate.\n50\t- **FIX-8 (anti-fabrication floor â€” resolves NS6 gameability) [v4-hardened]:** the slice done-check binds the\n51\t  end-to-end emitted statistic to the FIREWALL-VERIFIED module's output on the SAME input (tolerance-identical) â€”\n52\t  the recipe's reported number MUST equal Ramanujan's firewall'd function run on that input. PLUS a deterministic\n53\t  perturbation test (perturb input â†’ outputs change, known-sign where implied) as a secondary check. The BINDING\n54\t  (not perturbation alone) is what defeats input-proportional fabrication (e.g. output=f(input variance) with no\n55\t  ANOVA computed). FIX-8 does NOT claim to grade fidelity (honors R3); it guarantees the emitted numbers come\n56\t  from the verified analysis core, not a fabricated shortcut.\n57\t- **FIX-9 (per-skill done-floor â€” resolves Phases-1â€“5 under-specification):** EVERY cognitive skill's\n58\t  \"production depth = DONE\" is now concretely floored (see \"Per-skill done-floor\" below); Stage 2 sets the\n59\t  per-skill K/M.\n60\t- **FIX-10 (firewall-test independence â€” resolves self-authored unit tests):** Ramanujan emits the firewall's\n61\t  algorithm spec + unit tests in a context SEPARATE from (and before) the Phase-5 code that must satisfy them;\n62\t  the code build cannot edit those tests.\n63\t- **FIX-11 (prose-skill coverage path â€” resolves vacuous-green mismatch):** each validator declares (a manifest)\n64\t  which prose deliverables it graded, basename-linked so Foreman's vacuous-green guard sees real coverage; the\n65\t  P0.A Wave-0 spike MUST prove THIS prose-deliverable path passes, not just that a wrapped validator emits PASS.\n66\t- **FIX-12 [CORRECTED 2026-06-20]:** the program is NOT one monolithic Foreman plan that builds thin skills.\n67\t  Only **Phase 0 (shared infra)** is the immediate Foreman plan. **EACH cognitive skill is its OWN\n68\t  researchPrime deep-dive â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle**, where the best-in-class METHOD is\n69\t  searched/reviewed/refined and the skill's real protocol + canaries + non-goals are forged (a structural\n70\t  done-floor alone yields a generic, mediocre skill â€” the method must come from per-skill research). This\n71\t  restores the user's original cadence (\"multiple waves of researchPrime deep-dives + crucible specific for\n72\t  each wave, with a foreman follow on\"). The program sequence lives in `PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`; the recreate-a-\n73\t  paper proof + NS1 demo are their own cycles AFTER the skills exist. (Supersedes the earlier \"lightweight,\n74\t  one plan set\" reading, which wrongly stripped per-skill method depth.)\n75\t- **FIX-13 (NS1 is gated, not asserted) [v4-hardened]:** NS1 gets its OWN homed phase (Phase 7 below), not a\n76\t  floating note. Its criterion is REGRESSION-THEN-RECOVERY, not \"non-decrease\": inject a KNOWN defect into a\n77\t  built skill (a seeded regression that fails â‰¥1 specific canary), run a real sleep cycle, and require the\n78\t  distillation to RECOVER that canary to passing â€” a no-op/rollback revision CANNOT pass (it would leave the\n79\t  injected canary failing). This gates \"measurably IMPROVES\" (NS1), distinct from \"didn't regress\" (NS2).\n80\t- **FIX-14 (journal provenance â€” resolves seeded-vs-real-use):** build-time journal entries are captured from\n81\t  GENUINE dogfood/canary EXECUTIONS of the skill (provenance-tagged per R5), NOT hand-fabricated prose. The\n82\t  done-floor term is \"genuine-execution fixture entries,\" and the FIX-13 NS1 demonstration distills ONLY from\n83\t  genuine-execution-provenance entries (so the NS1 proof is not circular and honors the North Star's\n84\t  \"its own real-use experience\" + R5 provenance-distrust).\n85\t- **FIX-15 (advisory-judge isolation â€” resolves the single-command back-door):** the advisory cross-family/LLM\n86\t  run is a SEPARATE, failure-swallowed, output-segregated process whose exit code + stdout NEVER reach the\n87\t  wave's single gate command; an unreachable advisory host is a no-op on the gate. The P0.A Wave-0 spike MUST\n88\t  explicitly prove that an UNREACHABLE advisory host leaves the deterministic gate GREEN (not just that a\n89\t  wrapped validator emits PASS).\n90\t\n91\t## Per-skill done-floor (what \"production depth / DONE\" means for EACH of Phases 1â€“5)\n92\tA cognitive skill wave-group is DONE iff ALL (TAP-gated):\n93\t1. `NORTH-STAR.md` with â‰¥3 MACHINE-CHECKABLE non-goals (each a negative canary that must FAIL the skill).\n94\t2. A frozen canary set of â‰¥K DETERMINISTIC canaries covering the skill's core capability + every non-goal\n95\t   (K set per-skill at Stage 2; cross-family/LLM-judge canaries may be added as ADVISORY, never as the gate).\n96\t3. A `journal/` of â‰¥M GENUINE-EXECUTION fixture entries (captured from real dogfood/canary runs of the\n97\t   skill, provenance-tagged per R5 â€” NOT fabricated prose) in the 7-field schema (M per-skill at Stage 2).\n98\t4. All P0 gates GREEN (handoff contract, canary eval, drift checker) + map.json registered.\n99\t\n100\t## NS6 deterministic done-check (the proof's acceptance criterion â€” LOCKED at Stage 1)\n101\tThe recreate-a-paper slice PASSES iff ALL of:\n102\t1. Every stage boundary artifact (researchâ†’planâ†’build for the slice) passes the P0.B handoff contract gate\n103\t   (schema valid Â· all artifact_refs resolve on disk Â· north_star round-trips byte-identical Â· open_questions empty).\n104\t2. The understandâ†’build firewall artifacts EXIST and are linked: a frozen algorithm spec + unit tests\n105\t   emitted by Ramanujan, and the code satisfies those unit tests (TAP PASS).\n106\t3. The recipe emits a non-empty **Assumptions Ledger** (one row per recovered/assumed tacit value).\n107\t4. The recipe RUNS end-to-end and produces the reproduction's executed numbers, AND passes the FIX-8\n108\t   DETERMINISTIC perturbation test (perturb input data â†’ outputs must change, known-sign where implied) â€”\n109\t   this forces REAL computation without grading fidelity. A numeric-tolerance grader REPORT is present as\n110\t   ADVISORY (its verdict is recorded, NOT gated â€” PRINCIPLE-D).\n111\t5. The whole done-check is itself a TAP emitter returning all-pass from DETERMINISTIC conditions 1â€“4 only\n112\t   (so Foreman gates on real checks, not on a laundered advisory verdict).\n113\t\n114\t## North-Star criteria (every plan element must serve â‰¥1; the inclusion test)\n115\t- **NS1 self-improving:** a skill measurably improves from its own journal across a sleep cycle.\n116\t- **NS2 no-regression:** a sleep revision can never ship if it regresses the skill's frozen canary set.\n117\t- **NS3 no-drift:** a sleep revision that advances a machine-checkable non-goal is rejected.\n118\t- **NS4 model-agnostic:** persona = method + LOGICAL tier; swapping the tierâ†’model table repoints the fleet.\n119\t- **NS5 clean handoffs:** every stage boundary passes the machine-checkable handoff contract.\n120\t- **NS6 the proof:** the recreate-a-paper slice reproduces Gelman ANOVA and PASSES a deterministic\n121\t  architecture/handoff done-check (NOT graded on numeric fidelity).\n122\t\n123\t## Assumption map (premortem-derived; each has a mitigation in the phases)\n124\t- A1 *gemini-cli reachable for cross-family judging* â†’ MITIGATED by capability-gated branch (deterministic-only fallback; never silent same-family). [serves NS2/NS3]\n125\t- A2 *Foreman's test-gate substrate can host arbitrary canary suites* â†’ DERISKED by Phase-0 Wave 0 spike before any skill depends on it. [serves NS2]\n126\t- A3 *the eval harness is reusable across 3 validator types (R6)* â†’ DERISKED by building it as ONE harness + three pluggable check modules in Phase-0. [serves NS2/NS5/NS6]\n127\t- A4 *Gandalf-bootstrap (review engine reviewing itself)* â†’ BROKEN by gating Gandalf on deterministic canaries + cross-family judge built BEFORE it. [serves NS3]\n128\t- A5 *\"architecture/handoff success\" is definable deterministically* â†’ LOCKED in Phase-1 design as a concrete checklist (handoff gates pass + firewall artifacts exist + recipe emits Assumptions Ledger + end-to-end run completes). [serves NS6]\n129\t\n130\t## Phases (the master sequence)\n131\t\n132\t> **Sizing note (Shark 1 BLOCKER):** breadth-first makes this a LARGE plan set. It remains ONE Foreman\n133\t> plan set but is honestly multi-wave; Foreman auto-advances across waves with budget pre-flight + resume.\n134\t> Phase 0 alone is ~6 waves; each cognitive skill is ~1â€“2 waves; the slice ~2. Stage 2 decomposes them.\n135\t\n136\t### Phase 0 â€” Shared infrastructure (FIRST; everything below depends on it) â€” ~6 waves\n137\tThe cross-cutting machinery every skill wave reuses. Built ONCE, on the trio/Foreman substrate, Foundry\n138\tstays stateless.\n139\t- **P0.A Eval harness on Foreman substrate (R1/R2/R6) â€” opens with Wave-0 go/no-go spike (FIX-3):** the\n140\t  spike proves a wrapped validator emits TAP/pytest PASS events the Foreman gate counts (not vacuous-green).\n141\t  Go â‡’ build ONE harness + three validator modules ALL emitting TAP/pytest (FIX-1/4): (i) schema+path-existence\n142\t  (handoff), (ii) deterministic + cross-family canary eval (sleep/no-regression), (iii) numeric-tolerance\n143\t  grader (paper-repro). Cross-family judge via gemini-cli, capability-gated; FIX-7 fallback honesty.\n144\t  No-go fallback: validators run as a standalone Node test process Foreman shells to. [NS2,NS5,NS6]\n145\t- **P0.B Machine-checkable handoff contract (NS5):** formalize the contract schema (north_star round-trip,\n146\t  artifact_refs existence-check, block-on-open-questions, versioned persisted artifact); wire it as the\n147\t  reusable gate that Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md + Crucible's locate-plan.mjs both emit/validate.\n148\t- **P0.C Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table (NS1,NS3,NS4):** the per-skill repo skeleton â€”\n149\t  NORTH-STAR.md (purpose + machine-checkable non-goals as negative tests, R4 + invariants), SKILL.md,\n150\t  references/{journal-schema,improvement}.md, LESSONS.md, journal/ (append-only), CHANGELOG.md. Plus the\n151\t  NET-NEW logical-tierâ†’model **config table** (the brain seam) + a **swap test** (FIX-5): swapping the table\n152\t  changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits.\n153\t- **P0.D Journal + sleep loop (NS1,NS2,NS3,R5):** the 7-field journal schema; the sleep meta-recipe\n154\t  (clusterâ†’cross-context-corroborated distillâ†’North-Star gateâ†’eval-gateâ†’versioned promote w/ rollback).\n155\t  Distillation requires cross-context corroboration, provenance-distrust of unverified entries (R5).\n156\t- **P0.E Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning (FIX-6):** map.json entries + append-only invariant\n157\t  tests so canary SETS and templates are recorded as data/refs (Foundry stays stateless prose-only); drift\n158\t  checker stays GREEN. Canary sets are versioned ALONGSIDE skill versions; sleep may APPEND canaries, never\n159\t  edit/delete (deletion = human call).\n160\t- **P0.F Citation hygiene + provenance (R7):** correct SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670, drop/replace MemoryGraft in\n161\t  all carried docs; provenance fields in journal schema.\n162\t\n163\t### Phase 1 â€” Gandalf (critical review) â€” Wave 1 of the cognitive skills\n164\tFirst skill, because it is also the Review-stage engine for later waves. Gated by P0 infra (A4 broken).\n165\tPersona tier = top (Fable 5). Ships with its NORTH-STAR (non-goals as negative tests), a frozen canary set,\n166\tand a seeded journal. [NS1,NS2,NS3,NS6]\n167\t\n168\t### Phase 2 â€” Ramanujan (math/algorithm understanding)\n169\tBuilds the reasoning/algorithm graph the recipe's understandâ†’build firewall depends on. Tier = top. [NS6]\n170\t\n171\t### Phase 3 â€” Literature review (augmented researchPrime) â€” MOVED EARLY\n172\tUpstream lineage/lit-review is load-bearing for paper-repro (recovers tacit knowledge). Tier = Opus. [NS6]\n173\t\n174\t### Phase 4 â€” Data analysis (find/clean/analyze/report)\n175\tData pipeline + result comparison for the reproduction. Tier = Sonnetâ†’Opus. [NS6]\n176\t\n177\t### Phase 5 â€” Analytic + ML code (R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch) + Code verification (CO-DESIGNED)\n178\tCode generation/execution AND the fidelity firewall, designed together (code-verification is not bolted on\n179\tlast). Understandâ†’build firewall: frozen algorithm spec + unit tests from Ramanujan gate the code. Verify on\n180\tEXECUTED numbers w/ tolerance. Tier = Opus / Fable 5 for verification. [NS5,NS6]\n181\t\n182\t### Phase 6 â€” recreate-a-paper recipe (THE SLICE / PROOF)\n183\tComposes Phases 1â€“5. Required upstream lineage/lit-review; explicit Assumptions Ledger for tacit gaps;\n184\tunderstandâ†’build firewall; executed-number verification BOUND to the firewall module (FIX-8); context-isolated\n185\tcross-family grader (ADVISORY, FIX-15). GRADED on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (A5),\n186\treproducing Gelman ANOVA. [NS5,NS6 â€” the proof]\n187\t\n188\t### Phase 7 â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration (the self-improving proof) â€” ~1 wave\n189\tHomes FIX-13. Depends on: â‰¥1 built skill (Phase 1+) with its genuine-execution journal + the P0.D sleep loop.\n190\tInject a KNOWN defect (a seeded regression failing â‰¥1 named canary) into the chosen skill; run a real sleep\n191\tcycle (clusterâ†’distillâ†’North-Star gateâ†’eval gateâ†’versioned promote); REQUIRE the injected canary to recover\n192\tto passing AND all prior canaries to stay green (regression-then-recovery, FIX-13). Distills ONLY from\n193\tgenuine-execution-provenance entries (FIX-14). Deterministic, TAP-gated. [NS1 â€” the self-improving proof]\n194\t\n195\t## Out of scope (explicit, anti-drift)\n196\tGWL harness/t2rs brain (parallel track); stateful productivity/personal agents (later program phases);\n197\tthe extend-own-paper slice (second slice). Jumper/doc-writing/legal/propose-extensions = later waves.\n198\t\n199\t## Phasing rationale\n200\tPhase 0 is the single hard dependency: it removes the three adversarial blockers (eval-gate host,\n201\tcorrelated-authority, weak-proof) as INFRASTRUCTURE before any skill is built, so every later wave inherits\n202\ta hosted, cross-family-or-deterministic, machine-checkable gate. Skill order follows the recipe's data flow\n203\t(understand â†’ lineage â†’ data â†’ code+verify â†’ compose).\n204\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76ba0592-1eed-4333-9f77-187790b40902","uuid":"66caac57-a6a4-455b-badd-376d505204b7","timestamp":"2026-06-21T00:13:21.626Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/Skill Foundry/planning/portfolio-program/crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md","content":"# Portfolio Program â€” Master Plan (Crucible Stage 1)\n\n> North Star (LOCKED): Build a deep, self-improving skill repository in Skill Foundry â€” model-agnostic\n> cognitive skills, compositional recipes, and (later) stateful agents â€” where every skill carries a\n> LOCKED North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions\n> WITHOUT drifting from its designed purpose. First end-to-end proof: a recreate-a-paper recipe that\n> REPRODUCES the Gelman ANOVA paper, GRADED ON ARCHITECTURE/HANDOFF SUCCESS (not reproduction fidelity).\n\nThis Master Plan covers ONE Foreman-ready plan set, executed as sequential per-skill WAVE-GROUPS, whose\nFIRST executable wave is the Phase-0 shared infrastructure. Per-skill work here is lightweight (canary +\nNorth-Star authoring), NOT a full separate researchPrime cycle (FIX-12); full per-skill cycles are for\nLATER portfolio skills beyond this plan. The recreate-a-paper slice is the proof.\n\n> **Stage-1 Shark-Tank convergence (2026-06-20):** 3 Sharks found 3 â‰¥2-agree BLOCKERs + 2 MAJORs.\n> Scope fork resolved by the user (convergence authority): **BREADTH-FIRST** â€” this plan set builds all\n> five cognitive skills to production depth (full canary sets + journals), THEN the recreate-a-paper slice.\n> The four non-scope findings are folded into v2 below (see \"Shark-Tank fixes applied\").\n\n## Shark-Tank fixes applied (v2)\n- **FIX-1 (BLOCKER: Foreman gate can't host LLM-judge/numeric validators):** all three validator types\n  emit **Node-TAP / pytest output with real per-test PASS events** so Foreman's `runGate` counts them\n  (no vacuous-green HALT). The TAP/pytest emitter IS the shared interface (also resolves FIX-4).\n- **FIX-2 (BLOCKER: done-check not deterministic):** the architecture/handoff done-check is DEFINED NOW\n  (see \"NS6 deterministic done-check\" below), not deferred.\n- **FIX-3 (MAJOR: substrate spike has no gate):** P0.A opens with a **Wave-0 go/no-go spike** with an\n  explicit fallback if Foreman-substrate hosting of wrapped validators fails.\n- **FIX-4 (MAJOR: R6 shared interface unstated):** = the TAP/pytest emitter contract above.\n- **FIX-5 (MAJOR: NS4 tier table doesn't exist/untested):** the logical-tierâ†’model table is a NET-NEW\n  artifact built in P0.C **with a swap test** (swap the table â†’ assert the resolved model changes; no skill\n  prose edited). Replaces the scattered per-role TRIO_MODEL_<ROLE> env resolution.\n- **FIX-6 (carried: canary evolution):** canary sets are **versioned alongside skill versions**; a sleep\n  cycle may PROPOSE canary additions but never edit/delete existing canaries (append-only; a deletion is a\n  human call) â€” so the set neither ossifies (NS1) nor is silently weakened (NS2).\n- **FIX-7 (carried: A1 fallback honesty):** the deterministic-only fallback is valid ONLY for validator (iii)\n  and deterministic (ii) canaries; for LLM-judged (ii) canaries an unreachable cross-family host **HALTs as\n  a degraded-coverage stamp**, never silently scores same-family.\n\n## Shark-Tank fixes applied (v3 â€” round 2 convergence)\nRound 2 (substrate-verified) found the v2 gate was sound in plumbing but unsound in semantics. v3 folds\nONE governing principle + targeted fixes:\n\n- **PRINCIPLE-D (the deterministic-gate rule â€” resolves flaky-gate + HALT-incoherence):** the no-regression\n  GATE emits TAP `ok`/`not ok` ONLY from DETERMINISTIC checks (numeric tolerance, code/unit tests, path/schema\n  existence). **LLM-judge and cross-family judging are ADVISORY** â€” they write a report artifact recorded\n  alongside the wave, and NEVER emit a gate verdict. Consequences: (a) a non-deterministic judge can no longer\n  flip the gate GREENâ†”HALT (round-2 CLUSTER A); (b) an unreachable cross-family host can no longer HALT the\n  build â€” it just records \"degraded advisory coverage\" (corrects the false v2 FIX-7; Foreman HALT is terminal,\n  so judging must stay OUT of the gate path). The cross-family judge still runs when reachable; its value is a\n  recorded second-origin signal, not a gate.\n- **FIX-8 (anti-fabrication floor â€” resolves NS6 gameability) [v4-hardened]:** the slice done-check binds the\n  end-to-end emitted statistic to the FIREWALL-VERIFIED module's output on the SAME input (tolerance-identical) â€”\n  the recipe's reported number MUST equal Ramanujan's firewall'd function run on that input. PLUS a deterministic\n  perturbation test (perturb input â†’ outputs change, known-sign where implied) as a secondary check. The BINDING\n  (not perturbation alone) is what defeats input-proportional fabrication (e.g. output=f(input variance) with no\n  ANOVA computed). FIX-8 does NOT claim to grade fidelity (honors R3); it guarantees the emitted numbers come\n  from the verified analysis core, not a fabricated shortcut.\n- **FIX-9 (per-skill done-floor â€” resolves Phases-1â€“5 under-specification):** EVERY cognitive skill's\n  \"production depth = DONE\" is now concretely floored (see \"Per-skill done-floor\" below); Stage 2 sets the\n  per-skill K/M.\n- **FIX-10 (firewall-test independence â€” resolves self-authored unit tests):** Ramanujan emits the firewall's\n  algorithm spec + unit tests in a context SEPARATE from (and before) the Phase-5 code that must satisfy them;\n  the code build cannot edit those tests.\n- **FIX-11 (prose-skill coverage path â€” resolves vacuous-green mismatch):** each validator declares (a manifest)\n  which prose deliverables it graded, basename-linked so Foreman's vacuous-green guard sees real coverage; the\n  P0.A Wave-0 spike MUST prove THIS prose-deliverable path passes, not just that a wrapped validator emits PASS.\n- **FIX-12 [CORRECTED 2026-06-20]:** the program is NOT one monolithic Foreman plan that builds thin skills.\n  Only **Phase 0 (shared infra)** is the immediate Foreman plan. **EACH cognitive skill is its OWN\n  researchPrime deep-dive â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle**, where the best-in-class METHOD is\n  searched/reviewed/refined and the skill's real protocol + canaries + non-goals are forged (a structural\n  done-floor alone yields a generic, mediocre skill â€” the method must come from per-skill research). This\n  restores the user's original cadence (\"multiple waves of researchPrime deep-dives + crucible specific for\n  each wave, with a foreman follow on\"). The program sequence lives in `PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`; the recreate-a-\n  paper proof + NS1 demo are their own cycles AFTER the skills exist. (Supersedes the earlier \"lightweight,\n  one plan set\" reading, which wrongly stripped per-skill method depth.)\n- **FIX-13 (NS1 is gated, not asserted) [v4-hardened]:** NS1 gets its OWN homed phase (Phase 7 below), not a\n  floating note. Its criterion is REGRESSION-THEN-RECOVERY, not \"non-decrease\": inject a KNOWN defect into a\n  built skill (a seeded regression that fails â‰¥1 specific canary), run a real sleep cycle, and require the\n  distillation to RECOVER that canary to passing â€” a no-op/rollback revision CANNOT pass (it would leave the\n  injected canary failing). This gates \"measurably IMPROVES\" (NS1), distinct from \"didn't regress\" (NS2).\n- **FIX-14 (journal provenance â€” resolves seeded-vs-real-use):** build-time journal entries are captured from\n  GENUINE dogfood/canary EXECUTIONS of the skill (provenance-tagged per R5), NOT hand-fabricated prose. The\n  done-floor term is \"genuine-execution fixture entries,\" and the FIX-13 NS1 demonstration distills ONLY from\n  genuine-execution-provenance entries (so the NS1 proof is not circular and honors the North Star's\n  \"its own real-use experience\" + R5 provenance-distrust).\n- **FIX-15 (advisory-judge isolation â€” resolves the single-command back-door):** the advisory cross-family/LLM\n  run is a SEPARATE, failure-swallowed, output-segregated process whose exit code + stdout NEVER reach the\n  wave's single gate command; an unreachable advisory host is a no-op on the gate. The P0.A Wave-0 spike MUST\n  explicitly prove that an UNREACHABLE advisory host leaves the deterministic gate GREEN (not just that a\n  wrapped validator emits PASS).\n\n## Per-skill done-floor (what \"production depth / DONE\" means for EACH of Phases 1â€“5)\nA cognitive skill wave-group is DONE iff ALL (TAP-gated):\n1. `NORTH-STAR.md` with â‰¥3 MACHINE-CHECKABLE non-goals (each a negative canary that must FAIL the skill).\n2. A frozen canary set of â‰¥K DETERMINISTIC canaries covering the skill's core capability + every non-goal\n   (K set per-skill at Stage 2; cross-family/LLM-judge canaries may be added as ADVISORY, never as the gate).\n3. A `journal/` of â‰¥M GENUINE-EXECUTION fixture entries (captured from real dogfood/canary runs of the\n   skill, provenance-tagged per R5 â€” NOT fabricated prose) in the 7-field schema (M per-skill at Stage 2).\n4. All P0 gates GREEN (handoff contract, canary eval, drift checker) + map.json registered.\n\n## NS6 deterministic done-check (the proof's acceptance criterion â€” LOCKED at Stage 1)\nThe recreate-a-paper slice PASSES iff ALL of:\n1. Every stage boundary artifact (researchâ†’planâ†’build for the slice) passes the P0.B handoff contract gate\n   (schema valid Â· all artifact_refs resolve on disk Â· north_star round-trips byte-identical Â· open_questions empty).\n2. The understandâ†’build firewall artifacts EXIST and are linked: a frozen algorithm spec + unit tests\n   emitted by Ramanujan, and the code satisfies those unit tests (TAP PASS).\n3. The recipe emits a non-empty **Assumptions Ledger** (one row per recovered/assumed tacit value).\n4. The recipe RUNS end-to-end and produces the reproduction's executed numbers, AND passes the FIX-8\n   DETERMINISTIC perturbation test (perturb input data â†’ outputs must change, known-sign where implied) â€”\n   this forces REAL computation without grading fidelity. A numeric-tolerance grader REPORT is present as\n   ADVISORY (its verdict is recorded, NOT gated â€” PRINCIPLE-D).\n5. The whole done-check is itself a TAP emitter returning all-pass from DETERMINISTIC conditions 1â€“4 only\n   (so Foreman gates on real checks, not on a laundered advisory verdict).\n\n## North-Star criteria (every plan element must serve â‰¥1; the inclusion test)\n- **NS1 self-improving:** a skill measurably improves from its own journal across a sleep cycle.\n- **NS2 no-regression:** a sleep revision can never ship if it regresses the skill's frozen canary set.\n- **NS3 no-drift:** a sleep revision that advances a machine-checkable non-goal is rejected.\n- **NS4 model-agnostic:** persona = method + LOGICAL tier; swapping the tierâ†’model table repoints the fleet.\n- **NS5 clean handoffs:** every stage boundary passes the machine-checkable handoff contract.\n- **NS6 the proof:** the recreate-a-paper slice reproduces Gelman ANOVA and PASSES a deterministic\n  architecture/handoff done-check (NOT graded on numeric fidelity).\n\n## Assumption map (premortem-derived; each has a mitigation in the phases)\n- A1 *gemini-cli reachable for cross-family judging* â†’ MITIGATED by capability-gated branch (deterministic-only fallback; never silent same-family). [serves NS2/NS3]\n- A2 *Foreman's test-gate substrate can host arbitrary canary suites* â†’ DERISKED by Phase-0 Wave 0 spike before any skill depends on it. [serves NS2]\n- A3 *the eval harness is reusable across 3 validator types (R6)* â†’ DERISKED by building it as ONE harness + three pluggable check modules in Phase-0. [serves NS2/NS5/NS6]\n- A4 *Gandalf-bootstrap (review engine reviewing itself)* â†’ BROKEN by gating Gandalf on deterministic canaries + cross-family judge built BEFORE it. [serves NS3]\n- A5 *\"architecture/handoff success\" is definable deterministically* â†’ LOCKED in Phase-1 design as a concrete checklist (handoff gates pass + firewall artifacts exist + recipe emits Assumptions Ledger + end-to-end run completes). [serves NS6]\n\n## Phases (the master sequence)\n\n> **Sizing note (Shark 1 BLOCKER):** breadth-first makes this a LARGE plan set. It remains ONE Foreman\n> plan set but is honestly multi-wave; Foreman auto-advances across waves with budget pre-flight + resume.\n> Phase 0 alone is ~6 waves; each cognitive skill is ~1â€“2 waves; the slice ~2. Stage 2 decomposes them.\n\n### Phase 0 â€” Shared infrastructure (FIRST; everything below depends on it) â€” ~6 waves\nThe cross-cutting machinery every skill wave reuses. Built ONCE, on the trio/Foreman substrate, Foundry\nstays stateless.\n- **P0.A Eval harness on Foreman substrate (R1/R2/R6) â€” opens with Wave-0 go/no-go spike (FIX-3):** the\n  spike proves a wrapped validator emits TAP/pytest PASS events the Foreman gate counts (not vacuous-green).\n  Go â‡’ build ONE harness + three validator modules ALL emitting TAP/pytest (FIX-1/4): (i) schema+path-existence\n  (handoff), (ii) deterministic + cross-family canary eval (sleep/no-regression), (iii) numeric-tolerance\n  grader (paper-repro). Cross-family judge via gemini-cli, capability-gated; FIX-7 fallback honesty.\n  No-go fallback: validators run as a standalone Node test process Foreman shells to. [NS2,NS5,NS6]\n- **P0.B Machine-checkable handoff contract (NS5):** formalize the contract schema (north_star round-trip,\n  artifact_refs existence-check, block-on-open-questions, versioned persisted artifact); wire it as the\n  reusable gate that Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md + Crucible's locate-plan.mjs both emit/validate.\n- **P0.C Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table (NS1,NS3,NS4):** the per-skill repo skeleton â€”\n  NORTH-STAR.md (purpose + machine-checkable non-goals as negative tests, R4 + invariants), SKILL.md,\n  references/{journal-schema,improvement}.md, LESSONS.md, journal/ (append-only), CHANGELOG.md. Plus the\n  NET-NEW logical-tierâ†’model **config table** (the brain seam) + a **swap test** (FIX-5): swapping the table\n  changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits.\n- **P0.D Journal + sleep loop (NS1,NS2,NS3,R5):** the 7-field journal schema; the sleep meta-recipe\n  (clusterâ†’cross-context-corroborated distillâ†’North-Star gateâ†’eval-gateâ†’versioned promote w/ rollback).\n  Distillation requires cross-context corroboration, provenance-distrust of unverified entries (R5).\n- **P0.E Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning (FIX-6):** map.json entries + append-only invariant\n  tests so canary SETS and templates are recorded as data/refs (Foundry stays stateless prose-only); drift\n  checker stays GREEN. Canary sets are versioned ALONGSIDE skill versions; sleep may APPEND canaries, never\n  edit/delete (deletion = human call).\n- **P0.F Citation hygiene + provenance (R7):** correct SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670, drop/replace MemoryGraft in\n  all carried docs; provenance fields in journal schema.\n\n### Phase 1 â€” Gandalf (critical review) â€” Wave 1 of the cognitive skills\nFirst skill, because it is also the Review-stage engine for later waves. Gated by P0 infra (A4 broken).\nPersona tier = top (Fable 5). Ships with its NORTH-STAR (non-goals as negative tests), a frozen canary set,\nand a seeded journal. [NS1,NS2,NS3,NS6]\n\n### Phase 2 â€” Ramanujan (math/algorithm understanding)\nBuilds the reasoning/algorithm graph the recipe's understandâ†’build firewall depends on. Tier = top. [NS6]\n\n### Phase 3 â€” Literature review (augmented researchPrime) â€” MOVED EARLY\nUpstream lineage/lit-review is load-bearing for paper-repro (recovers tacit knowledge). Tier = Opus. [NS6]\n\n### Phase 4 â€” Data analysis (find/clean/analyze/report)\nData pipeline + result comparison for the reproduction. Tier = Sonnetâ†’Opus. [NS6]\n\n### Phase 5 â€” Analytic + ML code (R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch) + Code verification (CO-DESIGNED)\nCode generation/execution AND the fidelity firewall, designed together (code-verification is not bolted on\nlast). Understandâ†’build firewall: frozen algorithm spec + unit tests from Ramanujan gate the code. Verify on\nEXECUTED numbers w/ tolerance. Tier = Opus / Fable 5 for verification. [NS5,NS6]\n\n### Phase 6 â€” recreate-a-paper recipe (THE SLICE / PROOF)\nComposes Phases 1â€“5. Required upstream lineage/lit-review; explicit Assumptions Ledger for tacit gaps;\nunderstandâ†’build firewall; executed-number verification BOUND to the firewall module (FIX-8); context-isolated\ncross-family grader (ADVISORY, FIX-15). GRADED on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (A5),\nreproducing Gelman ANOVA. [NS5,NS6 â€” the proof]\n\n### Phase 7 â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration (the self-improving proof) â€” ~1 wave\nHomes FIX-13. Depends on: â‰¥1 built skill (Phase 1+) with its genuine-execution journal + the P0.D sleep loop.\nInject a KNOWN defect (a seeded regression failing â‰¥1 named canary) into the chosen skill; run a real sleep\ncycle (clusterâ†’distillâ†’North-Star gateâ†’eval gateâ†’versioned promote); REQUIRE the injected canary to recover\nto passing AND all prior canaries to stay green (regression-then-recovery, FIX-13). Distills ONLY from\ngenuine-execution-provenance entries (FIX-14). Deterministic, TAP-gated. [NS1 â€” the self-improving proof]\n\n## Out of scope (explicit, anti-drift)\nGWL harness/t2rs brain (parallel track); stateful productivity/personal agents (later program phases);\nthe extend-own-paper slice (second slice). Jumper/doc-writing/legal/propose-extensions = later waves.\n\n## Phasing rationale\nPhase 0 is the single hard dependency: it removes the three adversarial blockers (eval-gate host,\ncorrelated-authority, weak-proof) as INFRASTRUCTURE before any skill is built, so every later wave inherits\na hosted, cross-family-or-deterministic, machine-checkable gate. Skill order follows the recipe's data flow\n(understand â†’ lineage â†’ data â†’ code+verify â†’ compose).\n","numLines":204,"startLine":1,"totalLines":204}}}
