NEW logical-tierâ†’model config table built in P0.C with a swap test (swap table â†’ resolved model changes, zero skill-prose edits); replaces scattered `TRIO_MODEL_<ROLE>` env resolution (`:28-30`).\n- **FIX-6:** canary sets are versioned alongside skill versions; sleep may APPEND canaries but never edit/delete (deletion = human call) â€” so the set neither ossifies (NS1) nor is silently weakened (NS2) (`:31-33`).\n- **FIX-8 (v4-hardened):** the slice done-check **binds** the emitted statistic to the firewall-verified module's output on the same input (tolerance-identical), plus a deterministic perturbation test; the binding (not perturbation alone) defeats input-proportional fabrication. Does NOT grade fidelity (`:50-56`).\n- **FIX-12 (CORRECTED 2026-06-20):** the program is NOT one monolithic Foreman plan. Only **Phase 0 (shared infra)** is the immediate Foreman plan; **each cognitive skill is its own researchPrime â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman â†’ Learn cycle**, restoring the user's original multi-wave cadence (supersedes the earlier \"lightweight one plan set\" reading) (`:66-74`).\n- **FIX-13 (v4-hardened):** NS1 gets its own phase (Phase 7); its criterion is **regression-then-recovery**, not non-decrease â€” inject a known defect failing â‰¥1 canary, run a real sleep cycle, require recovery to passing (a no-op/rollback cannot pass) (`:75-79`).\n- **FIX-14:** build-time journal entries come from **genuine dogfood/canary executions** (provenance-tagged per R5), not fabricated prose; the NS1 demo distills only from genuine-execution entries (non-circular) (`:80-84`).\n- **FIX-15:** the advisory cross-family/LLM run is a separate, failure-swallowed, output-segregated process whose exit code/stdout never reach the wave's gate command; the P0.A Wave-0 spike must prove an unreachable advisory host leaves the gate GREEN (`:85-89`).\n\n## Per-skill done-floor (Phases 1â€“5, all TAP-gated)\nA cognitive skill wave-group is DONE iff: (1) `NORTH-STAR.md` with â‰¥3 machine-checkable non-goals as negative canaries; (2) a frozen set of â‰¥K deterministic canaries covering core capability + every non-goal; (3) a `journal/` of â‰¥M genuine-execution fixture entries in the 7-field schema; (4) all P0 gates GREEN + `map.json` registered. K/M set per-skill at Stage 2 (`:91-98`).\n\n## NS6 deterministic done-check (LOCKED at Stage 1)\nThe recreate-a-paper slice PASSES iff all of: (1) every stage boundary passes the P0.B handoff contract (schema valid Â· artifact_refs resolve Â· north_star round-trips byte-identical Â· open_questions empty); (2) firewall artifacts (frozen algorithm spec + unit tests from Ramanujan) exist and the code satisfies them (TAP PASS); (3) a non-empty Assumptions Ledger is emitted; (4) the recipe runs end-to-end producing executed numbers AND passes the FIX-8 perturbation test (tolerance grader is advisory only); (5) the done-check is itself a TAP emitter passing from deterministic conditions 1â€“4 only (`:100-112`).\n\n## Phase sequence\n- **Phase 0 â€” Shared infrastructure (~6 waves), the single hard dependency:** P0.A eval harness on Foreman substrate (opens with Wave-0 go/no-go spike) Â· P0.B handoff contract Â· P0.C repo templates + tierâ†’model table Â· P0.D journal + sleep loop Â· P0.E governance wiring + canary versioning Â· P0.F citation hygiene (correct SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670, drop MemoryGraft) (`:136-161`).\n- **Phases 1â€“5 (cognitive skills, recipe data-flow order):** Gandalf (critical review, also the Review engine, tier Fable 5) â†’ Ramanujan (math/algorithm, top) â†’ Literature review (augmented researchPrime, Opus, moved early) â†’ Data analysis (Sonnetâ†’Opus) â†’ Analytic+ML code + Code verification co-designed (Opus/Fable 5) (`:163-180`).\n- **Phase 6 â€” the slice/proof:** composes Phases 1â€“5, reproduces Gelman ANOVA, graded on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (`:182-186`).\n- **Phase 7 â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration (~1 wave):** homes FIX-13's regression-then-recovery proof (`:188-193`).\n\n## Anti-drift boundaries\n- **Out of scope (explicit):** GWL harness/t2rs brain (parallel track); stateful productivity/personal agents (later phases); the extend-own-paper second slice; Jumper/doc-writing/legal/propose-extensions (later waves) (`:195-197`).\n- Five North-Star criteria (NS1 self-improving Â· NS2 no-regression Â· NS3 no-drift Â· NS4 model-agnostic Â· NS5 clean handoffs Â· NS6 the proof) are the inclusion test; every plan element must serve â‰¥1 (`:114-121`).\n- Five assumptions (A1â€“A5) each carry a mitigation homed in a phase (e.g., A4 Gandalf-bootstrap broken by gating Gandalf on deterministic canaries + cross-family judge built before it) (`:123-128`).\n\n---\nOne caveat worth flagging: the document is internally honest that breadth-first makes this a **large, multi-wave** plan set (Phase 0 ~6 waves, each skill ~1â€“2, slice ~2), with decomposition deferred to Stage 2 (`:132-134,134`)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7806,"cache_read_input_tokens":29223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7806},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76ba0592-1eed-4333-9f77-187790b40902","uuid":"da5995fb-9922-482b-a94d-d94a1a5a0e25","request_id":"req_011CcFSPpAT5RHc9teEESzyP"}
